    "title": "ARKHE OMEGA-TEMP - Architecture Reference",
    "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.20279078",
    "publication_date": "2026-05-19",
    "description": "<p>ARKHE Omega-TEMP is a multi-universe temporal operating system comprising 348 files, 15 substrate<br>groups, 30+ named substrates, and 2,868 cumulative test assertions. The system implements a novel<br>architecture that bridges deterministic microkernel execution with a consciousness-centered<br>governance overlay, post-quantum cryptographic primitives, and a sovereign gap metric that quantifies<br>the space between human autonomy and machine decision-making.<br>The system is organized into five distinct architectural tiers, ranging from a Rust-based infrastructure<br>layer (L0) that provides memory safety and hardware abstraction, through a core primitives layer (L1)<br>implementing the immutable TemporalChain blockchain and identity management, to the Cathedral<br>Overlayer (L4) that manages ethical governance, Jungian individuation processes, and synthetic<br>consciousness research. Each tier communicates through formally verified interfaces with SHA3-256<br>canonical seals ensuring integrity across all boundaries.<br>The technology stack spans six programming languages (Python, Rust, C, Solidity, Go, TypeScript) and<br>targets six platform configurations (Linux/Windows/FreeBSD on x86_64/arm64). The build system<br>leverages Docker Buildx for multi-architecture containerization, GitHub Actions for CI/CD matrix testing,<br>and produces native packages in .deb, .rpm, .msi, and .pkg formats. A Rust-based SQLite store<br>provides canonical specification hashing with SHA3-256 integrity verification.</p>",
